&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Orkes is building the platform that powers the next generation of enterprise applications and AI systems. Founded by the creators of the open-source Netflix Conductor orchestration platform, Orkes helps organizations build, deploy, and operate mission-critical workflows and AI agents at massive scale. Our platform combines workflow and agent orchestration, integrations, observability, and resilience into a unified developer experience, enabling teams to build and operate complex deterministic and agentic workflows with confidence. From global enterprises to fast-growing startups, customers rely on Orkes to automate business-critical processes and execute billions of workflow and agent executions with the reliability, visibility, and fault tolerance required for production systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;h4 data-section-id=&quot;1vtzf0l&quot; data-start=&quot;397&quot; data-end=&quot;420&quot;&gt;About the Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone well-versed in Developer Community Engagement to drive our open-source community. This is a high-impact, externally-facing role for someone who genuinely loves the developer community and wants to help it grow around Orkes and Conductor.&lt;br&gt;This role sits at the intersection of community engagement, developer marketing, and technical content creation. You’ll help developers discover Orkes and aid them in successfully adopting the platform through high-quality technical education, community interaction, and advocacy. You’ll serve as a catalyst for increasing community engagement, fostering meaningful relationships, and creating programs that encourage participation, contribution, and long-term adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the perfect role for someone with a background in working with developer communities, a passion for technology, and excitement about helping create agentic transformation for developers and organizations. Ideally, you have a background in technical marketing, developer relations, or developer education and enjoy being externally visible to our community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p data-section-id=&quot;1f8nmp8&quot; data-start=&quot;1084&quot; data-end=&quot;1124&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interacting with developers via various online and in-person communities to drive awareness, engagement and usage of our products &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answer technical questions, unblock users, and foster an inclusive, knowledgeable, and strong community that developers want to be a part of&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Educate developers on workflow orchestration, agentic workflows, and distributed systems through your content and community programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build real relationships to empower our contributors, advocates, and power users&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create educational content such as blogs, tutorials, videos, walkthroughs, and learning materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end ownership of webinars, workshops, AMAs, demos, and community events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Orkes at conferences, meetups, podcasts, and online events&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring developer feedback back to Product and Engineering to help improve Orkes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-section-id=&quot;1biiopr&quot; data-start=&quot;1975&quot; data-end=&quot;2004&quot;&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p data-section-id=&quot;17ah4sd&quot; data-start=&quot;2006&quot; data-end=&quot;2022&quot;&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;2023&quot; data-end=&quot;2348&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;u0rquw&quot; data-start=&quot;2023&quot; data-end=&quot;2103&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2+ years of impactful experience in engagement with developers for deeply technical products in a community context&lt;/p&gt;
